{"term":"option","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:46d10d8ff81b56ad67","definition":"One of a set of choices that can be made.","example":"Luiz struggled with the movement of Helguson in the box, as he collected a long ball and the Spaniard barged him over, leaving referee Chris Foy little option but to point to the spot.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["alternative","choice","possibility","option","contingency"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antioption","antioptionist","binary option","co-option","credit default option","greenshoe option","local option","low exercise price option","multioption","negative option","network option time","non-option","not an option","nuclear option","optionable","optionaire","optional","optionary","option button","optionee","optioneering","optionless","optionlike","optionor","option-select","option type","preoption","reoption","Samson Option","Samson option"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/option#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:41d7570d0986c18d46","definition":"The freedom or right to choose.","example":"The marriage had not been contracted by the father, who was apparently dead, but by an agnatic guardian, so that it was liable to cancellation at the option of the girl on her attaining puberty.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["alternative","choice","possibility","option","contingency"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antioption","antioptionist","binary option","co-option","credit default option","greenshoe option","local option","low exercise price option","multioption","negative option","network option time","non-option","not an option","nuclear option","optionable","optionaire","optional","optionary","option button","optionee","optioneering","optionless","optionlike","optionor","option-select","option type","preoption","reoption","Samson Option","Samson option"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/option#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:53dbd79d85306f3ea6","definition":"A contract giving the holder the right to buy or sell an asset at a set strike price; can apply to financial market transactions, or to ordinary transactions for tangible assets such as a residence or automobile.","example":"There's a book out on us and there's gonna be a movie based on the book. ABC has bought the option for a movie to be made specially for T.V.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["alternative","choice","possibility","option","contingency"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antioption","antioptionist","binary option","co-option","credit default option","greenshoe option","local option","low exercise price option","multioption","negative option","network option time","non-option","not an option","nuclear option","optionable","optionaire","optional","optionary","option button","optionee","optioneering","optionless","optionlike","optionor","option-select","option type","preoption","reoption","Samson Option","Samson option"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/option#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c029b37559f4879d9b","definition":"The acquiring or retention of a nationality through personal choice as a right, bypassing selective legal mechanisms for naturalization, especially in cases where a territory is transferred or passed on from one state to another.","example":"At that time every emigrant who was made aware of such a notification submitted his application for option to the British Consuls within the period prescribed.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["alternative","choice","possibility","option","contingency"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["antioption","antioptionist","binary option","co-option","credit default option","greenshoe option","local option","low exercise price option","multioption","negative option","network option time","non-option","not an option","nuclear option","optionable","optionaire","optional","optionary","option button","optionee","optioneering","optionless","optionlike","optionor","option-select","option type","preoption","reoption","Samson Option","Samson option"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/option#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fb290a3a958528ce00","definition":"To purchase an option on something.","example":"The new novel was optioned by the film studio, but they'll probably never decide to make a movie from it.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antioption","antioptionist","binary option","co-option","credit default option","greenshoe option","local option","low exercise price option","multioption","negative option","network option time","non-option","not an option","nuclear option","optionable","optionaire","optional","optionary","option button","optionee","optioneering","optionless","optionlike","optionor","option-select","option type","preoption","reoption","Samson Option","Samson option"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/option#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:04f3f2991ae1482f8c","definition":"To configure, by setting an option.","example":"The device that is to echo the characters should be optioned for echoplexing.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["antioption","antioptionist","binary option","co-option","credit default option","greenshoe option","local option","low exercise